        {
          "description": "Ask the person for what only they have: a username, a password, a one-time code, a passkey touch, a CAPTCHA, a choice, a number, or a confirmation before an irreversible step (kind "verification": their bank wants them to confirm a payment in a banking app). For a sign-in, ask once for the username and password (kind login, input credentials), then any code (kind code, input secret), and type each yourself; do not ask the person to sign in in the browser. input: none (they do something, then press Done), text, secret (a code or password; type it with type_handoff_secret), credentials (a username, typed with type_text, and a password, typed with type_handoff_secret), choice (one of options), multi_choice (several of options), number (with constraints min/max/step/unit), confirm (approve or deny; risk "high" by default), scan (they scan or read what is on the screen with their phone, then press Done: a sign-in QR code the page shows, a number to match in an app, or Chrome's "use a phone or tablet" passkey QR code; kind passkey, login, verification or code; scan_source "page" for a code the page draws, "desktop" for Chrome's own passkey window; they see a live picture the server takes, never one you send), takeover (they take over the browser, then press Done: only for a passkey on this computer or a security key, a CAPTCHA you cannot pass, or when they declined to give a credential). Set the fields that do not apply to null. The run pauses until they answer.",
