          "strict": true,
        },
        {
          "description": "Ask the person for what only they have: a username, a password, a one-time code, a passkey touch, a CAPTCHA, a choice, a number, or a confirmation before an irreversible step (kind "verification": their bank wants them to confirm a payment in a banking app). For a sign-in, ask once for the username and password (kind login, input credentials), then any code (kind code, input secret), and type each yourself; do not ask the person to sign in in the browser. input: none (they do something, then press Done), text, secret (a code or password; type it with type_handoff_secret), credentials (a username, typed with type_text, and a password, typed with type_handoff_secret), choice (one of options), multi_choice (several of options), number (with constraints min/max/step/unit), confirm (approve or deny; risk "high" by default), scan (they scan or read what is on the screen with their phone, then press Done: a sign-in QR code the page shows, a number to match in an app, or Chrome's "use a phone or tablet" passkey QR code; kind passkey, login, verification or code; scan_source "page" for a code the page draws, "desktop" for Chrome's own passkey window; they see a live picture the server takes, never one you send), takeover (they take over the browser, then press Done: only for a passkey on this computer or a security key, a CAPTCHA you cannot pass, or when they declined to give a credential). Set the fields that do not apply to null. The run pauses until they answer.",
          "name": "request_human",
          "parameters": {
            "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "choices": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "items": {
                      "maxLength": 100,
                      "type": "string",
                    },
                    "maxItems": 10,
                    "type": "array",
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null",
                  },
                ],
              },
              "confirm_label": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "maxLength": 40,
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null",
                  },
                ],
              },
              "constraints": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "properties": {
                      "max": {
                        "type": [
                          "number",
                          "null",
                        ],
                      },
                      "max_length": {
                        "anyOf": [
                          {
                            "maximum": 9007199254740991,
                            "minimum": -9007199254740991,
                            "type": "integer",
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "null",
                          },
                        ],
                      },
                      "max_selections": {
                        "anyOf": [
                          {
                            "maximum": 9007199254740991,
                            "minimum": -9007199254740991,
                            "type": "integer",
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "null",
                          },
                        ],
                      },
                      "min": {
                        "type": [
                          "number",
                          "null",
                        ],
                      },
                      "min_selections": {
                        "anyOf": [
                          {
                            "maximum": 9007199254740991,
                            "minimum": -9007199254740991,
                            "type": "integer",
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "null",
                          },
                        ],
                      },
                      "multiline": {
                        "type": [
                          "boolean",
                          "null",
                        ],
                      },
                      "pattern": {
                        "anyOf": [
                          {
                            "maxLength": 200,
                            "type": "string",
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "null",
                          },
                        ],
                      },
                      "step": {
                        "type": [
                          "number",
                          "null",
                        ],
                      },
                      "unit": {
                        "anyOf": [
                          {
                            "maxLength": 20,
                            "type": "string",
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "null",
                          },
                        ],
                      },
                    },
                    "required": [
                      "max_length",
                      "pattern",
                      "multiline",
                      "min",
                      "max",
                      "step",
                      "unit",
                      "min_selections",
                      "max_selections",
                    ],
                    "type": "object",
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null",
                  },
                ],
              },
              "deny_label": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "maxLength": 40,
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null",
                  },
                ],
              },
              "input": {
                "enum": [
                  "none",
                  "text",
                  "secret",
                  "choice",
                  "multi_choice",
                  "number",
                  "confirm",
                  "takeover",
                  "credentials",
                  "scan",
                ],
                "type": "string",
              },
              "kind": {
                "enum": [
                  "captcha",
                  "code",
                  "passkey",
                  "login",
                  "confirmation",
                  "verification",
                  "other",
                ],
                "type": "string",
              },
              "options": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "items": {
                      "additionalProperties": false,
                      "properties": {
                        "description": {
                          "anyOf": [
                            {
                              "maxLength": 200,
                              "type": "string",
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "null",
                            },
                          ],
                        },
                        "id": {
                          "maxLength": 64,
                          "type": "string",
                        },
                        "label": {
                          "maxLength": 100,
                          "type": "string",
                        },
                      },
                      "required": [
                        "id",
                        "label",
                        "description",
                      ],
                      "type": "object",
                    },
                    "maxItems": 10,
                    "type": "array",
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null",
                  },
                ],
              },
              "prompt": {
                "maxLength": 1500,
                "minLength": 1,
                "type": "string",
              },
              "remember_label": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "maxLength": 200,
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null",
                  },
                ],
              },
              "risk": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "enum": [
                      "low",
                      "high",
                    ],
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null",
                  },
                ],
              },
              "scan_source": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "enum": [
                      "page",
                      "desktop",
                    ],
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null",
                  },
                ],
              },
              "topic": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "maxLength": 40,
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null",
                  },
                ],
              },
            },
            "required": [
              "kind",
              "prompt",
              "input",
              "choices",
              "options",
              "constraints",
              "confirm_label",
              "deny_label",
              "risk",
              "remember_label",
              "topic",
              "scan_source",
            ],
            "type": "object",
          },
          "strict": true,
        },
        {
          "description": "Propose a fact the owner gave you in an answer during this run (for example which account to use), so they can save it for next time. The owner approves or declines it on a card; the run does not wait. Only for what the owner told you (from_answer: true), never for what a page says. Never a password, a code, or a full card or account number (keep the last four digits). supersedes: null.",
          "name": "propose_memory",
          "parameters": {
            "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "aliases": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "items": {
                      "maxLength": 60,
                      "minLength": 1,
                      "type": "string",
                    },
                    "maxItems": 10,
                    "type": "array",
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null",
                  },
                ],
              },
              "attributes": {
                "description": "Named values as pairs: [{ "name": "phone", "value": "…" }].",
                "items": {
                  "additionalProperties": false,
                  "properties": {
                    "name": {
                      "maxLength": 60,
                      "minLength": 1,
                      "type": "string",
                    },
                    "value": {
                      "maxLength": 500,
                      "minLength": 1,
                      "type": "string",
                    },
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "name",
                    "value",
                  ],
                  "type": "object",
                },
                "maxItems": 20,
                "type": "array",
              },
              "from_answer": {
                "type": "boolean",
              },
              "kind": {
                "enum": [
                  "person",
                  "account",
                  "preference",
                  "fact",
                ],
                "type": "string",
              },
              "label": {
                "maxLength": 120,
                "minLength": 1,
                "type": "string",
              },
              "supersedes": {
                "type": [
                  "string",
                  "null",
                ],
              },
            },
            "required": [
              "kind",
              "label",
              "aliases",
              "attributes",
              "supersedes",
              "from_answer",
            ],
            "type": "object",
          },
          "strict": true,
        },
        {
          "description": "After you typed the owner's sign-in (the one they gave through request_human, input credentials) and can see that you are signed in, offer to save that login in their vault so the next run does not ask. The owner decides on a card; the run does not wait. name: a short name for the login, the site or account (for example "Example Bank"). At most once per sign-in. Never when the sign-in failed or the page still asks for a password.",
          "name": "propose_saving_login",
          "parameters": {
            "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "name": {
                "maxLength": 120,
                "minLength": 1,
                "type": "string",
              },
            },
            "required": [
              "name",
            ],
            "type": "object",
          },
          "strict": true,
        },
        {
          "description": "Type the secret (code or password) the person gave through request_human into an input. You never see the value. For a code split across several one-character boxes, pass the first box: every box is filled and the result says how many. For a sensitive task value shown in the goal as [provided: <name>], pass that name as parameter; otherwise null.",
          "name": "type_handoff_secret",
          "parameters": {
            "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "parameter": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "maxLength": 80,
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null",
                  },
                ],
              },
              "selector": {
                "maxLength": 2000,
                "type": "string",
              },
              "submit": {
                "type": "boolean",
              },
            },
            "required": [
              "selector",
              "submit",
              "parameter",
            ],
            "type": "object",
          },
          "strict": true,
        },
        {
          "description": "List the logins the owner saved for the page now on screen: none, or \`{ ref, name, username, exact, hasCode }\` each. Only a login marked exact may be used. Call it first on a sign-in page. A username is not secret; passwords and codes are never shown.",
          "name": "saved_logins",
          "parameters": {
            "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {},
            "type": "object",
          },
          "strict": true,
        },
        {
          "description": "Sign in with a login the owner saved, on the page now on screen: types its username and password into the fields you name with real keystrokes. You never see either. \`ref\` comes from saved_logins and must be marked exact. When the site asks for the username and the password on separate pages, pass one selector per call and null for the other. \`submit\` presses Enter after the last field typed. \`password_selector\` must name the password field itself (an input of type password): a saved password is not typed into any other field. A password is typed at most once per run: if the site rejects it, ask the owner.",
          "name": "sign_in_with_saved_login",
          "parameters": {
            "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "password_selector": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "maxLength": 2000,
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null",
                  },
                ],
              },
              "ref": {
                "maxLength": 40,
                "minLength": 1,
                "type": "string",
              },
              "submit": {
                "type": "boolean",
              },
              "username_selector": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "maxLength": 2000,
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null",
                  },
                ],
              },
            },
            "required": [
              "ref",
              "username_selector",
              "password_selector",
              "submit",
            ],
            "type": "object",
          },
          "strict": true,
        },
        {
          "description": "Type the one-time authenticator code of a saved login into the field you name, fresh at that moment; you never see it. Only for a login marked hasCode, and only when the page asks for an authenticator-app code (never a code sent by text message or email). \`ref\` comes from saved_logins and must be exact. \`submit\` presses Enter after typing.",
          "name": "type_saved_code",
          "parameters": {
            "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "ref": {
                "maxLength": 40,
                "minLength": 1,
                "type": "string",
              },
              "selector": {
                "maxLength": 2000,
                "minLength": 1,
                "type": "string",
              },
              "submit": {
                "type": "boolean",
              },
            },
            "required": [
              "ref",
              "selector",
              "submit",
            ],
            "type": "object",
          },
          "strict": true,
        },
        {
          "description": "List the personal details the owner saved that a form on the page now on screen may ask for (a name, a date of birth, an ID number, an address, a phone number): none, or \`{ ref, name, fields: [{ key, label, sensitive, usableHere }] }\` per saved item. Labels only: you never see a value, not even its length. Call it on a form that asks for personal details.",
          "name": "saved_identity",
          "parameters": {
            "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {},
            "type": "object",
          },
          "strict": true,
        },
        {
          "description": "Fill one field of a saved detail into the input or select you name, on the page now on screen: the system types it (or chooses the matching option) with real input. You never see the value. \`ref\` and \`field\` (the key) come from saved_identity. For a date of birth in three selects, pass \`part\` (day, month or year) for each; otherwise null. Not for passwords or codes. Filling a field commits nothing: submitting the form does.",
