          "strict": true,
        },
        {
          "description": "Type a saved card into the checkout form, after declare_charge: the system types the number, then the expiry, the name and the postal code, and the security code last, with real input; you never see them. \`ref\` comes from saved_cards. For each field the form has, give where it is: a selector, or x and y for a field inside an embedded payment frame (a card number box that is part of another site's frame). \`expiry\` is one combined MM/YY input; use exp_month and exp_year when they are separate. number is required; give security_code only if the form asks for it and saved_cards says it is allowed; null for the rest. Typing the card commits nothing: pressing the pay button does. Pressing it needs the owner's approval, which the system has recorded for this amount.",
